## Frontend Pages

All pages live in `artifacts/clinical-trials/src/pages/`.

### `/` — Dashboard
- Summary cards: regulatory doc counts (Current/Expiring Soon/Expired)
- Quick links to other sections

### `/documents` — Regulatory Documents
- Table of all docs with name, expiration date, days remaining, status badge
- "Sync to Calendar" button → `POST /regulatory/sync-calendar`

### `/reports` — Sponsor Reports
- **Generate Report** button (triggers staleness modal if needed)
- **Concurrent guard banner** — shown when another report is already active
- **Staleness warning modal** — shown when sheet is 24h+ old, requires acknowledgment
- **Status bar** — current report status with action buttons:
  - Draft → [Send to PI] [Discard]
  - PI Review → [Mark Approved]
  - Approved → [Mark Final]
- **Unreplaced placeholder warning** — shown if any `{{...}}` remain after fill
- **Report history list** — all past reports with status, date, doc link

### `/settings` — Settings
All fields saved to Replit DB via `PUT /api/settings`:

| Field | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| Notion Regulatory DB ID | Notion database ID for regulatory documents |
| Notion AE Log DB ID | Notion database ID for adverse events |
| Notion Deviation Log DB ID | Notion database ID for protocol deviations |
| Google Sheets ID | File ID of the EDC enrollment extract sheet |
| Sheet Tab Name | Tab name (default: Sheet1) |
| Header Row Number | 1-based row number of the header (default: 1) |
| Google Docs Template ID | File ID of the report template |
| PI Email | Principal Investigator's email address |
| Sponsor Email | Sponsor's email (for future use) |
| Google Calendar ID | Calendar ID (default: primary) |
| **Sponsor Call Event ID** | Google Calendar event ID for the sponsor call — report link is appended here on finalization. To find it: open event in Google Calendar → Edit → URL contains `eid=` param (base64-encoded). Decode at base64decode.org to get the raw event ID. |
| Nag Interval (hours) | Hours between PI reminder emails (default: 4) |

